2025-05-01 04:12:59 - Thread-66 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• "week": date of the Google‑Trends week – used to keep only records between 2024‑09‑01 and 2024‑09‑14 and to restrict to weekdays (Mon–Fri).  
• "rank": numeric popularity rank – filter to the top three ranks (1, 2, 3).  
• "term": the actual Google‑Trends query – the item we ultimately want to list.  
• "refresh_date": date the record was last refreshed – used to GROUP BY and to ORDER BY (descending).  
• "dma_id", "dma_name", "score": optional descriptive fields that can be shown or aggregated if needed.

Conditions that will be useful  
• "week" BETWEEN '2024‑09‑01' AND '2024‑09‑14'  
• DAYOFWEEK("week") BETWEEN 2 AND 6    -- Snowflake: 1=Sun … 7=Sat  
• "rank" IN (1,2,3)

Ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows)

```sql
--Description: Preview any TOP_TERMS rows whose “week” falls in the required two‑week window.
SELECT *
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: Show only weekday (Mon–Fri) rows for the same period.
SELECT "week", "term", "rank", "refresh_date"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
  AND DAYOFWEEK("week") BETWEEN 2 AND 6
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: Verify how many weekday rows possess top‑three ranks.
SELECT "week", "term", "rank"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
  AND DAYOFWEEK("week") BETWEEN 2 AND 6
  AND "rank" IN (1,2,3)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: List distinct refresh_date values present in the target slice.
SELECT DISTINCT "refresh_date"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
  AND DAYOFWEEK("week") BETWEEN 2 AND 6
ORDER BY "refresh_date" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: Retrieve term, rank and refresh_date for every top‑three record, ordered by refresh_date DESC then rank ASC.
SELECT "refresh_date", "week", "term", "rank"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
  AND DAYOFWEEK("week") BETWEEN 2 AND 6
  AND "rank" IN (1,2,3)
ORDER BY "refresh_date" DESC, "rank" ASC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: Count how many top‑three terms exist per refresh_date to confirm grouping cardinality.
SELECT "refresh_date", COUNT(*) AS "cnt_top3_terms"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
  AND DAYOFWEEK("week") BETWEEN 2 AND 6
  AND "rank" IN (1,2,3)
GROUP BY "refresh_date"
ORDER BY "refresh_date" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: Aggregate the three terms for each refresh_date into a comma‑separated string.
SELECT
  "refresh_date",
  LISTAGG("term", ', ') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY "rank") AS "top3_terms"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
  AND DAYOFWEEK("week") BETWEEN 2 AND 6
  AND "rank" IN (1,2,3)
GROUP BY "refresh_date"
ORDER BY "refresh_date" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: Bring in DMA information while still keeping only the top‑three weekday terms.
SELECT "refresh_date", "week", "dma_name", "term", "rank"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
  AND DAYOFWEEK("week") BETWEEN 2 AND 6
  AND "rank" IN (1,2,3)
ORDER BY "refresh_date" DESC, "rank" ASC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: Show distinct weekday names present in the slice (Mon, Tue, …) using TO_CHAR for clarity.
SELECT DISTINCT TO_CHAR("week", 'DY') AS "weekday"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
  AND DAYOFWEEK("week") BETWEEN 2 AND 6
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: Final style query—deliver refresh_date, weekday, term and rank for the needed set, fully ordered.
SELECT
  "refresh_date",
  TO_CHAR("week", 'DY') AS "weekday",
  "term",
  "rank"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
  AND DAYOFWEEK("week") BETWEEN 2 AND 6
  AND "rank" IN (1,2,3)
ORDER BY "refresh_date" DESC, "rank" ASC
LIMIT 20;
```
